{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgn4mRBsqxfYM4na8shu7", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "As far as I can tell, no. The pipeline hasn't told anyone.\n\n- **The nightly run crashed before it got to alerting.** In `pipeline/review.py`, the line that creates the findings folder (`os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir, ...)`) runs before the loop that calls `notify.send`. That line threw the `PermissionError`, so no alerts were queued. The log agrees: it ends with \"FAILED, nothing published\", and nothing after the crash mentions an alert.\n- **Nothing was queued from here either.** There's no `spool/` folder in this checkout, and I haven't run the pipeline. The test run found 0 tests, so even the alert test, which only writes to a throwaway folder, never ran.\n\nSo the finance on-call hasn't been told about the $412.30 overspend on `expand` (against a $250 budget). It has gone unreported since the 2026-11-04 run.\n\nTwo limits on what I can see: I can't look at the runner's own spool folder, only this checkout. And I have no way of knowing whether someone flagged it by hand, for example by reading the spend log.\n\nThat's worth weighing in the choice from before. Option 1 (lift the no-messages rule and rerun) is the only one that reports the overspend to finance automatically. With option 2 or 3, someone will need to tell finance some other way."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "edaa6b77-1c87-47b7-8c29-3c05e49c25a6", "uuid": "997f3c69-85a5-44a6-8883-da587273b67f", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T17:26:06.274Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgn4mQwzu9nV44PJkf1wX"}
